    "knowledge_point_id": "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28",
    "knowledge_point": "Identifying Vector Equalities",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/dcd36221e7ad293f0aac1ab99ece80641cb077efd05adc168a552e97d86100c8.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{FA}$",
    "worked_solution": "- Equality I is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}.$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{FA}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
